### Docker Dev Container

This project runs its agent tooling inside a container. The bind-mounted
project directory is your host filesystem; named volumes keep auth and
caches across restarts. The image follows this project's own
`harness.config.env` (package manager, agent CLI, LaTeX, GPU) — after
re-running `init_harness.py` to reconfigure, run `docker compose build`
again to pick up a changed `Dockerfile`. The container's default foreground
process is [herdr](https://herdr.dev), a terminal workspace manager for AI
coding agents, installed unconditionally alongside whichever agent CLI(s)
this project enabled. See `harness/USER_GUIDE.md` §12 for the full
workflow, including reconfiguring mounts.

```bash
docker compose build                # build the image
docker compose up -d                # start the container, detached
docker compose attach harness       # attach to the running herdr TUI
# or, for a plain shell instead:
docker compose exec harness bash
docker compose down                 # stop it (project dir untouched)
```
